                <pb facs="0845" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1232: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Paraguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Horn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-24T11:00:00-03:50">June 24, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>61. My 60, June 23, 11 a.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d569-f1"/> Reply of Paraguayan
                    Government dated yesterday and delivered to Bolivian Minister this morning
                    expresses regret that Bolivia’s request for discrediting Ynsfran should have
                    been coupled by threat to suspend diplomatic relations. Paraguayan note
                    considers incident complained of as of slight consequence and refuses to comply
                    with Bolivia’s request. I am told text of both Bolivian and Paraguayan notes
                    will be published in today’s papers.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
